    "primaryWitnesses": [
      {
        "ref": "2KI 3:3",
        "textualBasisJa": "Nevertheless he held to the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, with which he made Israel to sin. He didn’t depart from them."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 9:9",
        "textualBasisJa": "I will make Ahab’s house like the house of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, and like the house of Baasha the son of Ahijah."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 10:29",
        "textualBasisJa": "However, Jehu didn’t depart from the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, with which he made Israel to sin—the golden calves that were in Bethel and that were in Dan."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 10:31",
        "textualBasisJa": "But Jehu took no heed to walk in the law of the LORD, the God of Israel, with all his heart. He didn’t depart from the sins of Jeroboam, with which he made Israel to sin."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 13:2",
        "textualBasisJa": "He did that which was evil in the LORD’s sight, and followed the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, with which he made Israel to sin. He didn’t depart from it."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 13:6",
        "textualBasisJa": "Nevertheless they didn’t depart from the sins of the house of Jeroboam, with which he made Israel to sin, but walked in them; and the Asherah also remained in Samaria.)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 13:11",
        "textualBasisJa": "He did that which was evil in the LORD’s sight. He didn’t depart from all the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, with which he made Israel to sin; but he walked in them."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 14:24",
        "textualBasisJa": "He did that which was evil in the LORD’s sight. He didn’t depart from all the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, with which he made Israel to sin."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 15:9",
        "textualBasisJa": "He did that which was evil in the LORD’s sight, as his fathers had done. He didn’t depart from the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, with which he made Israel to sin."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 15:18",
        "textualBasisJa": "He did that which was evil in the LORD’s sight. He didn’t depart all his days from the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, with which he made Israel to sin."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 15:24",
        "textualBasisJa": "He did that which was evil in the LORD’s sight. He didn’t depart from the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, with which he made Israel to sin."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 15:28",
        "textualBasisJa": "He did that which was evil in the LORD’s sight. He didn’t depart from the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, with which he made Israel to sin."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 17:21",
        "textualBasisJa": "For he tore Israel from David’s house; and they made Jeroboam the son of Nebat king; and Jeroboam drove Israel from following the LORD, and made them sin a great sin."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 17:22",
        "textualBasisJa": "The children of Israel walked in all the sins of Jeroboam which he did; they didn’t depart from them"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 23:15",
        "textualBasisJa": "Moreover the altar that was at Bethel and the high place which Jeroboam the son of Nebat, who made Israel to sin, had made, even that altar and the high place he broke down; and he burned the high place and beat it to dust, and burned the Asherah."
      }
    ],
